# Commits that moved whitespace and nothing else, so that `git blame`
# attributes each line to the change that last said something about it
# rather than to the reformat that last re-wrapped it.
#
# GitHub's blame view honours this file automatically. Locally it is one
# command, once per checkout:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Only add a commit here that a reviewer could have merged blind: a
# formatter's output over files nobody else touched in it. A commit that
# also changed behaviour must not be listed, because blame would then
# skip past the line that introduced it.

